Post VRAM without an owning CUDA context.

NIXL 1.5.0 moved descriptor posting onto the libfabric progress thread
(upstream PR #1949), and that thread now fails a transfer when it cannot
apply the CUDA context captured at registration. Device memory mapped
with the CUDA VMM API (cuMemAddressReserve + cuMemCreate + cuMemMap)
belongs to no context, so cuPointerGetAttributes reports a NULL one; the
backend captured that NULL, and every VRAM post then failed with
NIXL_ERR_BACKEND.

Treat a NULL owning context the way the backend already treats a
multi-GPU process: report it from cudaUpdateCtxPtr so the engine turns
the context workaround off and the progress thread calls cudaSetDevice
for each descriptor's device instead. The device comes from the
descriptor, not from whatever context the registering thread happens to
hold, which matters for one-agent-per-GPU processes. The progress thread
consults one process-wide mediator, so this relies on the most recently
constructed engine having registered VMM memory; the general
no-usable-context fallback is tracked in GEX-4312.

TODO(GEX-4312): propose this upstream and drop the patch once it lands.

diff --git a/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp b/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp
--- a/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp
@@ -278,6 +278,13 @@
         return -1;
     }
 
+    // Memory mapped with the CUDA VMM API (cuMemCreate + cuMemMap) is owned by
+    // no context, so cuPointerGetAttributes reports a NULL one. There is no
+    // context to apply on the progress thread; take the cudaSetDevice path.
+    if (ctx == NULL) {
+        return -1;
+    }
+
     if (pthrCudaCtx_) {
         if (pthrCudaCtx_ != ctx) {
             return -1;
@@ -1000,8 +1007,9 @@
             if (use_cuda_addr_wa) {
                 bool need_restart;
                 if (vramUpdateCtx((void *)mem.addr, mem.devId, need_restart)) {
-                    NIXL_INFO << "Multi-GPU detected (device " << mem.devId
-                              << "), using cudaSetDevice fallback";
+                    NIXL_INFO << "Address for device " << mem.devId
+                              << " has no owning CUDA context or spans devices,"
+                                 " using cudaSetDevice fallback";
                     {
                         const std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(cuda_ctx_mutex_);
                         cuda_addr_wa_ = false;
